sec.p:
To examine overturning variability, we analyze pre-industrial control (piControl) simulations from nine coupled climate models participating in the sixth phase of the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project (CMIP6) (17; Supplementary Table 1) and one high-resolution climate model used in Yeager et al. (2021)15. These models provide the required diagnostics and span a range of model formulations and horizontal resolutions. The spatial configuration of our study is mainly based on the geography of the OSNAP observing system, which spans the subpolar North Atlantic across a full section (O-Full) composed of two coast-to-coast subsections, O-West and O-East (Fig. 1a).Fig. 1Mean and variability of the overturning streamfunction in density space using CESM2.
