Consistent with OSNAP observational estimates13, overturning at O-West is markedly weaker than at O-East, spans a narrower density range, and peaks at a higher density (Fig. 1b). Turning to the zonally integrated overturning streamfunction, the southward-flowing lower AMOC limb, with waters denser than \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
