To examine temporal relationships between upstream and downstream variability, lead–lag correlations are computed throughout this study. In these cases, correlations are evaluated over a range of positive and negative lags, with negative lags indicating subpolar transport leading the downstream MOC. The maximum correlation across all lag times is reported, and the corresponding lead-lag times vary among models and are shown in the Supplementary Information (e.g., Supplementary Fig. 11). Correlation profiles are first calculated independently for each model, then aligned in density space (with respect to \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
