Surface-forced water mass transformation (SFWMT) was computed offline in density space following the standard Walin framework and using the same formulation as in previous studies of subpolar overturning variability15,23. Briefly, monthly surface heat and freshwater fluxes were combined with surface temperature and salinity to obtain the surface density flux, which was then integrated over the outcrop area of each density class to yield transformation as a function of density. The calculation used the monthly model fields hfds, wfo, tos, and sos, and was performed on the same density grid as the overturning analysis (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
